\[\|\mathbf{PC}\|^2 = \|\mathbf{CD}\|^2 - \|\mathbf{PD}\|^2 = (t \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 6 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}) \cdot (t \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 6 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}).\]Thus,
\begin{align*}
\frac{d}{dt} \|\mathbf{PC}\|^2 &= (t \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 6 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}) \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 6 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= -2 \|\mathbf{PC}\|^2 + (-32t + 41) \\
&= -2 \|\mathbf{PC}\|^2 - 2a,
\end{align*}where $a = 16t - \frac{41}{2}.$  Then
\[\frac{a}{\|\mathbf{PC}\|^2} = -8t = \frac{PC}{PD}.\]Finally,
\[\|\mathbf{PC}\|^2 + \left( \frac{PC}{PD} \right)^2 = \left( \frac{3}{2} PD \right)^2 = \frac{9}{4} PD^2.\]We substitute $PC\|^2 = \frac{4}{9} PD^2 - PD^2 = -\frac{5}{9} PD^2$ to get
\[-\frac{4}{3} PD^2 = -PA^2 = \left( \frac{PD - PA}{2} \right)^2 = \frac{PA^2}{4},\]which gives us $PD = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} PA.$  Thus,
